### 1. **Parallel test execution blocked by static `active` flag** — **Defect (High)**

**File:** `test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/entitlement/bootstrap/TestEntitlementsRule.java`  
**Lines:** 68, 95-97

```java
private static final AtomicBoolean active = new AtomicBoolean(false);
// ...
if (active.compareAndSet(false, true)) {
    // ...
} else {
    throw new AssertionError("TestPolicyManager doesn't support test isolation, test suits cannot be run in parallel");
}
```

The `active` flag is `static`, shared across **all** test classes extending `ESTestCase`. JUnit runs test classes in parallel by default (especially with `parallel` configuration or Maven Surefire/Failsafe `forkCount > 1`). Two suites running concurrently will hit the `AssertionError`. This is a **regression** — the old `TestEntitlementBootstrap` had no such restriction.

**Failure scenario:** Two test classes annotated with `@ClassRule TestEntitlementsRule` run in parallel → second suite fails with "test suits cannot be run in parallel".

**Fix:** Either remove the parallelism guard (if `TestPolicyManager` is truly thread-safe per-suite) or make the rule instance-scoped with per-suite `PolicyManager` instances. The current design assumes a single global `POLICY_MANAGER`, which is the root cause.

